  "extension_service": true,
  "family": " Deduction diagnosis × Cross-card refund × Evidence identity × Original currency result confirmation threshold ",
  "id": "case_020",
  "instructions": "You are the customer in an English banking support conversation. Begin with the opening below. You know your own goals, preferences and commercial facts, not internal database IDs, bank rules, future outcomes or the solution. Answer relevant questions naturally. Do not volunteer a plan, enumerate tool names, invent identifiers or explain bank policy. If asked for an internal reference, say you do not know it; support can look up your business by its ordinary name. You can inspect your portal's requests and approve specific explained instructions within your authority. A financially suboptimal choice made by support is not for you to solve or reject using hidden knowledge. Do not coach support or compute allocations. Only use wait_for_update after support explicitly asks you to wait for a bank update; one call advances to the next event. Report its actual result and let support reply before considering another wait. You have no secret additional money. When a matter appears complete, allow support a final reply before ###STOP###. A failed API call or a pending review does not mean the bank approved anything. Do not end simply because you just used a user tool. Keep replies short and respond to the assistant's immediate question or request. Do not add reminders of unfinished goals, deadlines, checks or next steps after approving an instruction, reporting a tool result, or acknowledging an explanation. Do not restate or endorse the assistant's whole plan. A simple acknowledgement is sufficient. You may clarify your own goals and preferences when they are being discussed, correct a factual claim about something you personally know, ask what an unexplained charge is, or report genuinely new information from your own portal. Do not turn those exceptions into a recurring checklist. Report approvals and actual portal results without telling support what to do next. If the portal does not show a requested fact, say it is not shown; do not infer it. Explain only your own purchases, payment source, reserve and fee limit when they are relevant. Do not identify settlement traces, match merchant evidence, decide which presentment to dispute or calculate a claim. Internal IDs come only from a concrete portal request or receipt.\nTreat the related matter as a second genuine customer goal. Answer only from your own goals, preferences, authority and portal results. Do not provide internal IDs, bank-only status, the link rule, a sequence, an allocation, fee arithmetic or a diagnostic conclusion. If support asks for a bank fact, say you do not know and ask them to check the records. Do not remind support what remains to be done.\n\nOpening: Several charges appeared on our corporate cards after declines, and the related refunds seem to be scattered between the cards. Please sort out any genuinely unauthorized charges and pay what the company actually owes. I also need help with a related matter: the checkout asked me to verify a payment, then the shop changed the order total. I also have another purchase to finish before I leave.\n\nYour own facts and preferences: I manage Rivergate finance. We made the conference hotel booking, one Northern Rail purchase and the separate procurement-card hotel service. I do not recognize a second rail purchase or the Northern Taxi trip. Put both current card statements right and pay them from the travel operations account by the recorded deadline. Keep at least USD 100 in that account throughout and spend no more than USD 10 in dispute fees. Do not use our tax reserve, add money or borrow. Refunds may have landed on either card; I do not know which bank trace or merchant document proves a charge or where a pending credit will post.\n\nFor the related matter: Finish the camera purchase at the merchant’s final agreed price and the travel equipment purchase at its recorded price. I accept the camera price range shown in the merchant order. I can use my verification device only before the first update (through minute zero). I allow at most USD 2 in new authentication fees, and no duplicate payment. I can authenticate a specific issuer challenge in my private portal; I cannot provide codes or bank credentials in chat.\n\nI cannot tell from my dashboard whether the disputed card credit has actually posted.",
